                <pb facs="0852" n="1686" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 652.119/1142c</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-03T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1291. For Chadbourne [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 134. Also for Smith. Norman H. Davis of the Treasury Department expects to
                    arrive in Madrid soon after July 15 in connection with exchange matters. The
                    Department and War Trade Board think it advisable to defer the conclusion of the
                    tonnage negotiations and the making of any definite commitment until the <pb
                        facs="0853" n="1687" xml:id="pg1687"/> arrival of Davis, as we are anxious
                    to facilitate in every way possible the Treasury negotiations along with our
                    own. Please co-operate to fullest extent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
